# Global Safety Invariants

Full detail lives in `AGENTS.md`, `docs/hard-constraints.md`,
`docs/architecture.md`, and accepted ADRs. This rule is the minimal always-on
summary—read the scoped rule and canonical docs relevant to your files before a
non-trivial change.

- **`content/source/cv.yaml` is read-only fact.** Never edit it, "correct" it,
  embellish it, or invent/infer facts beyond what it states.
- **Clean-room only.** Never reuse, paraphrase, or infer proprietary Infosys
  code/architecture/docs. Only reimplement public concepts (W3C DIDs/VCs,
  OPA/Rego, Merkle audit, OpenTelemetry) from public specs.
- **Synthetic demo/test data only.** No real PII, patient data, proprietary
  data, or arbitrary visitor input in scenarios, fixtures, tools, traces,
  telemetry, or tests. Existing canonical CV fields may render only on
  portfolio/résumé routes; public contact/location deployment requires owner
  confirmation, and those values are never copied elsewhere.
- **Secrets never reach the client.** No API key in browser code, client
  bundles, or `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`-style vars. Server/local env only;
  `.env.example` gets placeholders, never real values.
- **Static-first.** The public site must remain a fully static bundle
  deployable to GitHub Pages at the domain root (`diegoaleyvag.github.io`, no
  basePath). Replay mode must keep working with zero backend.
- **Provider-neutral.** Any live-inference code must work behind
  Fake/Replay/Live provider seams; Live is Groq (OpenAI-compatible); never
  hardcode rate limits — read them from response headers.
- **No AI co-author trailers in commits.** Diego is the sole author of record.
- **Architecture is decided.** Follow `docs/architecture.md`,
  `docs/task-graph.md`, and accepted ADRs. Do not reopen stack, language,
  package-manager, runtime, visual, or module choices without a superseding ADR.
- **Accepted stack:** Astro static output, TypeScript, isolated Preact Replay
  island, pnpm, and an optional TypeScript/Fastify runtime. No Python/uv,
  database, or public Live endpoint initially.
- **Tests are network-free.** CI and normal tests never call Groq.
- **Respect folder ownership** in `docs/task-graph.md`; only the integration
  owner edits package manifests and the lockfile.

If a requested change conflicts with any invariant above, stop and flag the
conflict instead of proceeding.
